## Why This Is Asked

This question probes ability to design end-to-end scalable ingestion with strong isolation and cost discipline, plus onboarding automation.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation strategies (namespaces, resource groups)
- Ingestion options (IoT Hub vs Event Hubs) and scaling
- Data encryption with CMK and Key Vault
- RBAC, Service Principals, least privilege
- Onboarding automation (ARM/Bicep/Terraform), CI/CD
- Monitoring, auditing, budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo onboarding snippet (illustrative only)
async function onboardTenant(tenantId){
  await createEventHubNamespace(`tenant-${tenantId}-eh`);
  await createStorageAccount(`tenant${tenantId}sa`);
  await assignRBAC(tenantId, 'Contributor');
  await configureCMK(`tenant-${tenantId}-cmk`);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test isolation boundaries at scale?
- What are the trade-offs of per-tenant storage vs a shared data lake with tagging?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-region data residency, cross-subscription CI/CD, and security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Cosmos DB with RLS and multi-region writes
- API Management as API facade
- Azure Front Door for global routing and TLS termination
- Terraform + GitHub Actions across subscriptions
- Data residency and backup strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Terraform-like snippet (HCL/Terraform)
provider "azurerm" {
  features = {}
}
resource "azurerm_cosmosdb_account" "example" {
  name                = "example-cosmos"
  location            = "East US"
  locations           = [
    { location_name = "East US" },
    { location_name = "West Europe" }
  ]
  kind                          = "GlobalDocumentDB"
  enable_multiple_write_locations = true
  consistency_policy            = { consistency_level = "Session" }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test DR failover and data latency?
- How would you enforce per-tenant data access at API level?
- How would you monitor cost and usage across regions?
